  "description": "The high-performance road bike of your dreams. Stage race geometry, excellent acceleration, fearless handling.\nProduction sizes\nProduction frame\nHYAK: Our handmade production race frame.\n(HI-yak) Chinook word meaning \"fast\" or \"quick\".\nHand built in our Portland shop, the Hyak represents a quarter century of elite level bike racing -- training, coaching, fitting, frame building -- distilled into a smooth, responsive, and lightweight production frame. The high-performance road bike of your dreams. Stage race geometry, excellent acceleration, fearless handling. No racks, no fenders, no compromises, just a classic race bike with comfortable and stable handling that inspires confidence.\nSPECS:\nSloping top tube frame design yields a compact and dynamic ride with plenty of standover.\nTraditional down tube braze-ons for shifter or cable stop bosses. Available in Di2/eTap/EPS configuration.\nTraditional reinforced 1-1/8\" head tube, and single oversized main tubes paired with 24mm chain stays and 14mm seat stay.\nTraditional English 68mm bottom bracket.\nTraditional 27.2mm seatpost.\nRemovable aluminum seat post clamp.\nStandard single color powder coat with single color decals. Custom paint available.\nFrame weights from 4 lb. for a 56cm.\nAvailable in 2cm sizes from 50-62cm.\nAvailable as a complete bike with any component build.\nRitchey cast drop-outs for light weight, strength and rigidity.\nClearance for 28mm tires.\nSplit stop brake cable routing makes for easy maintenance and stronger rear braking.",
